2|0@progun^1440969416#cul4nci:Sturmgewehr90$:I think we've heard this many times before, but the issue of gun rights is a culture war. Places like the UK and AU are predominantly anti-gun because their society gradually deemed guns unnecessary to the point where the guys in government don't need to convince anyone to be anti-gun anymore. It's still possible, however difficult it may be, to reverse that by re-expanding gun culture. I know I don't really have any credibility to tell other people in other places what to do with themselves, but at least here in California, there is some hope. CA didn't used to be so anti-gun, you know? Some decades ago, it was as pro-gun as pro-gun could be. Hell, for the fact that CA is both physically and occupationally massive, there is a huge saturation of gun owners in this state who just happened to have been born into a poor change in management. As bad as it got here, the anti-gun presence in CA is simply a loud vocal minority albeit a powerful one. I've been thinking about this for a long while now, but I wonder what would happen if almost every Californian gun owner suddenly just decided to switch off their bullet buttons simultaneously? Still, you have a point. I'm just a little bit optimistic about it. I think I have no choice but to be optimistic. Leaving CA isn't an option so I believe I should do what I can. There do exist some workarounds, so we're not completely helpless. It might be different up in Canada, but I sincerely hope things turn out for the better, neighbor. I'm still a little jelly about not being able to get a SIG PE90. Those things are slick as fuuuüuck.
